<div class="wp-block-group"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"style":{"typography":{"fontWeight":"600","letterSpacing":"-0.01em"}},"fontSize":"2-xl"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-2-xl-font-size" style="font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em">Who Palmhurst still suits</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted-foreground","fontSize":"base"} -->
<p class="has-muted-foreground-color has-text-color has-base-font-size">Palmhurst is a dependable board for a single depot running a fixed weekly rota. It covers the basics well: jobs get created, assigned and closed without much ceremony, and a new dispatcher can learn it in an afternoon. The ceiling appears once you add a second depot, subcontracted crews or same-day changes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"style":{"spacing":{"blockGap":"var:preset|spacing|3"}},"layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"style":{"typography":{"fontWeight":"600","letterSpacing":"-0.01em"}},"fontSize":"2-xl"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-2-xl-font-size" style="font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em">What to weigh before you move</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted-foreground","fontSize":"base"} -->
<p class="has-muted-foreground-color has-text-color has-base-font-size">Count the hours your dispatchers spend rebuilding routes by hand, then compare that with the cost of the seats you would add. Ridgeway earns its keep on the days that go wrong, when a van breaks down at ten and eleven appointments have to be resequenced before lunch. If those days are rare for you, the simpler board is the honest answer.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->
